    'kakao.t': 'Ask on KakaoTalk', 'kakao.add': '💬 Add KakaoTalk channel', 'kakao.chat': 'Open channel →', 'kakao.s': 'Add the AidPage KakaoTalk channel and ask in plain words: "Gwanak-gu warnings", "emergency texts", "shelter", "find support". Answers use the same public data as this site; conversations are not stored.',
    'where.empty': 'Detailed data for this area is not available yet. It will open here as data is prepared.', 'where.formula': 'How the numbers are computed',
    'about.p1': 'Disaster support in Korea is scattered across five layers — the Act, the Presidential Decree annex, ministry notices, indirect support from 17 agencies, the relief-fund rules and insurance law — and no public screen shows all 38 items for your situation at once (surveyed 2026-08). Damage must be reported within 10 days of the disaster end (Decree art. 9②), and the people least likely to know that deadline are the most vulnerable.', 'about.p2': 'Public administration calls this <b>administrative burden</b> — learning costs, compliance costs and psychological costs (Herd &amp; Moynihan 2018). AidPage tries to move that burden from the citizen to the system.', 'about.n1': 'We do not adjudicate. Every result is "possible eligibility"; the municipality decides.', 'about.n2': 'We collect no personal data. Inputs are computed in your browser and exist only in the share URL. Resident reports alone are kept on a server (Cloudflare) for 7 days, text only, no names or phone numbers. For improvement we count anonymous usage (how often each screen is used) — never what you entered or where you are.', 'about.n3': 'We show no unverified numbers. Every amount carries its legal basis, date and source; we never invent coordinates; military facilities are not shown.', 'about.d1': 'Boundaries: Statistics Korea SGIS administrative dong (vuski/admdongkor, CC BY 4.0), simplified.', 'about.d2': 'Weather and warnings: KMA forecast and warning APIs. Fine dust: AirKorea. Emergency texts: Safety Data platform. Collected every 30 min (once keys are registered).', 'about.d4': '18 facility types (shelters, cooling/warming centers, community centers, ERs, pharmacies, fire, police, meal sites, water, hazard points): SafeKorea facility map, data.go.kr standard datasets, LocalData, OpenStreetMap (ODbL).', 'about.d5': 'Local-risk grid (258 districts nationwide, H3 ~0.1 km²): MOIS nationwide flood-trace maps and Seoul flood-trace maps 2010–2025, MOIS landslide records, Copernicus GLO-30 surface model, MOIS resident registration (dong), straight-line walk estimate to civil-defence shelters. Colours are within-district quintiles, not absolute risk; no record does not mean safe.', 'about.d3': 'Support rules: Framework Act on Disaster and Safety Management §66; Regulation on Cost-Sharing Standards for Natural Disaster Relief and Recovery (amended 2025-11-27) Annex 1, §9, §12; Relief Fund Management Regulation; storm & earthquake insurance subsidy standards.', 'about.b1': 'The anonymous question-first entry is borrowed from DisasterAssistance.gov (US), "one number + expandable basis" from First Street, and the risk formulas from FEMA BCA and Korea’s MD-FDA. Map tiles: OpenFreeMap · © OpenStreetMap.', 'about.f1': 'Personal project · non-profit', 'about.h1': 'Method and limits', 'about.why': 'Why', 'about.not': 'What we don’t do', 'about.data': 'Data and updates', 'about.borrow': 'Credits', 'about.rules': 'View all rules',
