    'grid.title': 'Local risks', 'grid.nodata': 'No data', 'grid.note': 'H3 cells (~0.1 km²). Colours are a <b>relative 5-class split within this district</b>, so they cannot be compared across districts. Grey cells have no data.', 'grid.rel': 'relative 5 classes within district', 'grid.how.t': 'How these figures are made · limits', 'grid.how': '<ul class="how"><li><b>Flood history</b> — MOIS nationwide flood-trace maps and Seoul flood-trace maps (2010–2025). Only reported/surveyed floods are included: <b>no record does not mean safe.</b> Seoul data are denser, so more history is captured there.</li><li><b>Landslide history</b> — MOIS landslide occurrence records; same limit.</li><li><b>Slope · elevation</b> — Copernicus GLO-30 surface model (30 m); building and tree heights are included, so urban slopes may be overstated.</li><li><b>Population · elderly living alone</b> — MOIS resident registration by administrative dong; the dong value is stamped on every cell of that dong, so do not add cells together. May differ from actual residence.</li><li><b>Walk to shelter</b> — straight-line distance from cell centre to the nearest civil-defence shelter ÷ 67 m/min. Roads and slope are not modelled.</li><li><b>Colour classes</b> — quintiles of cell values within the selected district. Not an absolute risk level; not for ranking or comparing districts.</li><li><b>Empty attributes</b> — semi-basement share, buildings 30y+ and 100-year flood risk await data approval.</li></ul>',
